            "paragraph": "In the dry season, biomass burning is prevalent throughout the basin. The most intense burning and atmospheric perturbations take place at the southern and eastern edges of the vast forest. Local fire emissions as well as basin-wide background pollution also affect the Manaus region during this time period. Wet deposition also decreases during the dry season. As a result of these spatial and temporal differences, cloud-aerosol-precipitation interactions are significantly different between the two seasons (Andreae et al., 2004; Feingold et al., 2005; Artaxo et al., 2013).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
